<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Open</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>open &lt;item&gt;
open &lt;door&gt;
open &lt;direction&gt; &lt;door&gt;
</pre>
<p>Examples:
</p>
<pre>open chest
open door
open east gate
</pre>
<p>Opens something that is closed: a chest, a bag, a coffin, or a door, gate 
or hatch on the way out of a room. Doors are named by a keyword, such as 
door or gate; if there are several, add the direction.
</p><p>A locked thing won't open: unlock it first (see <a cmd='#'>Help Lock</a>). Opening a 
door opens it on both sides, and those on the other side see it open.
</p><p>You can also open something you are shut inside, such as a coffin, from 
the inside, unless you have been buried in it: then call for help (see 
<a cmd='#'>Help Knock</a>). You can open things while sitting or resting, but not 
asleep.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Close</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Lock</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Knock</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Exits</a>
</pre>




</div>